/workspace/wt/codex/docs/validation_policy.md:59:Public replay ancestry shared with an inherited policy must be disclosed.
/workspace/wt/codex/docs/v5_validation_report.md:22:The expanded replay library, corrected sale estimator, longer advance horizons, and joint worker assignment were evaluated and not included when they failed to improve the wider selection panel. The estimator correction is technically accurate, but the legacy heuristics need joint retuning around the corrected signal. No neural PPO model was trained or deployed in this round.
/workspace/wt/codex/docs/v5_validation_report.md:28:The seed audit found no overlap between these panels, the 387 world seeds in earlier recorded research plans, or the 95 downloaded public replay worlds. This removes direct world reuse; it does not remove shared policy ancestry.
/workspace/wt/codex/docs/v5_validation_report.md:113:95 unique public games were downloaded and replayed to their exact recorded final balances. The 79/16 whole-episode library split exported 158 training streams, but teacher overlap and inherited library ancestry remain. Some excluded games were inspected as diagnostics; they are not an untouched generalization test.
/workspace/wt/codex/docs/v5_selection_ledger.md:21:final sale-block reordering, correction confined to the replay forecaster,
/workspace/wt/codex/docs/v5_research_notes.md:39:production plan, deeper timing tuned on tiny samples, spliced replay routes,
/workspace/wt/codex/docs/v5_research_notes.md:84:The read-only collection contains 95 unique public episodes: our listed losses,
/workspace/wt/codex/docs/v5_research_notes.md:87:The library excludes 16 episodes selected by a stable episode hash and exports
/workspace/wt/codex/docs/v5_research_notes.md:89:turns, products, quantities and observed shop context. It never exports replay
/workspace/wt/codex/docs/v5_research_notes.md:94:Some excluded episodes are inspected as diagnostics and therefore are not an
/workspace/wt/codex/docs/v5_research_notes.md:96:reacting games; more replay data is not automatically better.
/workspace/wt/codex/docs/v5_research_notes.md:110:[Evgen Dvorkin's replay analysis](https://www.kaggle.com/code/evgendvorkin/kaggriculture)
/workspace/wt/codex/docs/v5_research_notes.md:123:replay patterns. No candidate or harness changes during a run; no early stop
/workspace/wt/codex/docs/stability_report.md:27:The panel contains Meta v4, Idle, Wonder and Shop Router. These have public replay/tape ancestry and must not be counted as four independent strong strategic families.
/workspace/wt/codex/docs/stability_report.md:87:**5,752/5,752 actions matched across eight actual non-self public replays.** Four are v3 losses and four are early v4 wins. Self-validation episodes were excluded using submission IDs. This checks deployed behavior; the selected sample is not an unbiased win-rate estimate.
/workspace/wt/codex/docs/stability_report.md:98:None of the four sampled winning replays had early animal losses or failed placements. This is useful diagnostic contrast but remains a tiny, selected sample with different opponents. The large real-game loss regimes are poorly represented by the easier local public panel; more clone games cannot resolve that coverage gap.
/workspace/wt/codex/docs/stability_report.md:102:The previous builder could rerank existing episodes into different splits when downloads expanded the collection. Existing plans now preserve membership and assignments. Extraction rejects split/configuration drift. Training reads only planned episodes, ignores unrelated cache files, and rejects mismatched split labels, unverified reconstructions or duplicate replay hashes. Eight regression tests passed.
/workspace/wt/codex/docs/stability_report.md:104:The original dataset remains **36 train / 12 validation / 12 test games**, with no duplicate replay hashes found. Twelve of the seventeen test-team display names also appear in training; ten of eleven test winning-teacher names appear among training winners. Those are name-based proxies, before rating filtering, not stable policy IDs. Whole-game separation therefore does not establish generalization to unseen teachers. No new model was trained or promoted in this audit.
/workspace/wt/codex/docs/stability_report.md:106:A full load through the corrected training path reproduced the prior cleaned worker datasets exactly in size: **62,443 training / 24,497 validation / 17,675 test examples**, with 212 features. The winning-teacher rating filter retains 28/11/8 episodes respectively; these are subsets of the frozen 36/12/12 episode allocation. This check loaded data only; it did not fit another model.
